I've been doing some thinking (instead of playing hack) lately, and I
wondered what people would think of a "Scroll of Information."
Essentially, it's like a big fortune cookie, and it tells you
something that is actually useful.

For example, there were my recent questions on temples. I knew about
#offering sacrifices, but that was it. It would be nice to come across
a scroll saying:

----------

  You may do several different things on an altar. These include:

    1. #offer blah you have blah
    2. drop objects to detect whether they are blah
    3. blah for an blah
    4. Blah blah

  If the altar is not of your alignment, then you can blah blah blah,
  and it may blah!

  Also, when in a temple, you may blah blah blah with the priest, and
  he will blah blah for you.

-----------

Naturally, the "blah" would be replaced with the real information. I'm
trying not to give anything away here.

Why? Because there is an awful lot of information that just can't be
gotten by playing the game, which is critical or at least very useful.
Not everyone has access to rec.games.hack, or can ftp the tip sheets,
so this would be a good way of handling it.

Problems -- this would mean more files that would have to be typed up
by somebody on the development team, and they would sit around taking
up system space. The files might also be subject to abuse, if people
were able to read them freely. And, Murphy's law says that you would
probably get the same darn information every time.

Possibilities -- instead of having separate files, the scroll of
information could just read n lines out of some spoiler file, selected
at random, so the player might just get partial information, and might
get a real gold mine.

These scrolls would probably be quite rare.

A blessed scroll of information could do several things. Maybe it
would read a couple of info files, or a longer segment of the spoiler
file. Or it might be guaranteed to read one of the
extra-special-valuable info files. Or maybe it would just turn into a
blank scroll after the info was read.

A cursed scroll of information might give misinformation (which would
mean more files... gack), or it might be "smudgy" (missing/changed
characters, like partially erased graffiti), or maybe it would just
use the fortune cookie file.

Just a suggestion, since everyone seems to have them. :-)
